Patch-Source: https://github.com/IdentityPython/pysaml2/pull/977

pyOpenSSL 26.4.0 removed X509Req, X509Extension, dump_certificate_request,
load_certificate_request and crypto.verify, which breaks saml2.cert
(OpenSSLWrapper) and saml2.sigver.active_cert at runtime.

Backport of the still-unmerged upstream PR that replaces pyopenssl (and
python-dateutil) with cryptography.  Only difference from the PR: the
sigver.py import block is left in the upstream master style instead of
re-introducing the importlib_resources fallback and a duplicate
"from urllib import parse".

